# Bustle {4}{R/G}{R/G} (CR 107.4e, 708.8): "Creatures you control get +2/+2 and gain trample until end of turn. You may turn a creature
# you control face up." Bot1 has two face-down Faerie Snoops (cast for {3} on turns 1 and 3) and an Ornithopter; Bot2 has a face-down
# Snoop and an Ornithopter. On turn 5 Mox Ruby and Mox Emerald pay the two hybrid symbols and Black Lotus (black) and Mox Pearl the {4}.
# Only a creature of Bot1's that is face down is offered: its Ornithopter (face up) and Bot2's face-down Snoop (not Bot1's) are refused,
# and so are two at once ("a creature"). Turning the first Snoop up triggers its "look at the top two cards": Bot1 takes Ancestral
# Recall and Lightning Bolt goes to the graveyard. Bustle pumped every creature of Bot1's, the turned-up one included (it is the same
# permanent, CR 708.8): Ornithopter 2/4, Snoop 3/6 face up, the other Snoop a face-down 4/4, all with trample; Bot2's stay 0/2 and 2/2.

